<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Takaungu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Takaungu is a small coastal town in Kilifi County, Kenya, north of Mombasa. After the Busaidi of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oman">Oman</a> took Mombasa in 1837, a branch of the Mazrui family settled there and ruled it as a semi-independent town. Some of its leaders joined the Mazrui rebellion against British rule in 1895–1896.</p></div>
